STORE INFORMATION SHOWN WITH THE QUESTION:
[1] Store FAQ (Care and safety). How should I store a watch I don't wear often? In its box, away from direct sunlight, magnets and damp. Solar watches should be stored face-up in light.

[2] Store FAQ (Care and safety). Can I wear my watch in a sauna or hot shower? No. Heat and steam can damage the seals of any water-resistant watch.

[3] Store FAQ (Care and safety). Can I wear my watch in the gym? Yes, but rinse metal, rubber and silicone straps after heavy sweating and keep leather straps dry.

